      },
      "remediation": {
        "action": "Review bucket policy Principal elements for external account IDs. Remove statements granting access to accounts not in your organization. Use aws:PrincipalOrgID condition to restrict access to your AWS Organization.",
        "description": "Bucket policy grants access to external AWS accounts outside your organization. Cross-account access may be unintended.",
        "example": "{\n  \"storage\": {\n    \"kind\": \"bucket\",\n    \"access\": {\n      \"has_external_access\": false\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "asset_id": "vuln-wildcard-policy",
      "asset_type": "aws_s3_bucket",
      "asset_vendor": "aws",
      "control_compliance": {
        "nist_800_53_r5": "AC-6"
      },
      "control_compliance_ccm_v4": [
        "DSP-17",
        "IAM-16"
      ],
      "control_description": "S3 bucket policies must not grant access to a wildcard principal (Principal \"*\" or AWS: \"*\"). A wildcard principal makes every statement in the policy effectively anonymous or cross-account unless a restricting Condition (aws:PrincipalOrgID, aws:SourceVpc, aws:SourceIp with a fixed CIDR, aws:SourceArn, etc.) narrows it. Without such a Condition, the policy is a public-access grant regardless of which specific S3 actions are allowed.\n",
      "control_id": "CTL.S3.ACCESS.002",
      "control_name": "No Wildcard Principal Policies",
      "control_severity": "high",
      "evidence": {
        "first_unsafe_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
        "last_seen_unsafe_at": "2026-01-11T00:00:00Z",
        "misconfigurations": [
          {
            "actual_value": "[SANITIZED]",
            "operator": "eq",
            "property": "storage.access.has_wildcard_principal",
            "unsafe_value": true
          },
          {
            "actual_value": "[SANITIZED]",
            "operator": "eq",
            "property": "storage.kind",
            "unsafe_value": "bucket"
          }
        ],
        "root_causes": [
          "general"
        ],
        "temporal_risk": "Asset non-compliant for 240 hours (SLA: 168 hours). Exposed since 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z.",
        "threshold_hours": 168,
        "unsafe_duration_hours": 240
      },
      "exposure": {
        "principal_scope": "public",
        "type": "wildcard_principal"
      },
      "finding_id": "sha256:39aa8d4a21c81d37",
      "posture_drift": {
        "exposure_window_count": 1,
        "pattern": "persistent"
      },
      "remediation": {
        "action": "Replace the wildcard principal with the specific AWS account IDs or ARNs that need access, or add a restricting Condition on aws:PrincipalOrgID, aws:SourceVpc, aws:SourceIp (with a fixed CIDR), or aws:SourceArn. If the bucket genuinely needs to be public (CDN origin, static asset bucket), narrow the Actions to the minimum set and keep Public Access Block enabled where compatible.",
        "description": "Bucket policy contains a statement with a wildcard principal. Unless a Condition restricts the caller, any AWS identity or anonymous caller can invoke the statement's allowed actions.",
        "example": "{\n  \"storage\": {\n    \"kind\": \"bucket\",\n    \"access\": {\n      \"has_wildcard_principal\": false\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      }
    },
